xnu 0144: clear the TCS enable bits before a second vote

The ldoc7 vote never ran: the ldoc2 vote left CMD_ENABLE at 1 (the driver
clears those bits itself, the hardware does not), so the second rail saw the
TCS busy and bailed out. Clear the bits and reuse the TCS.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_touch.c
@@ -509,9 +509,14 @@
 	    MONDRIAN_RSC_ACTIVE_TCS, idle,
 	    mondrian_tlmm_read(rsc, base + MONDRIAN_RSC_STATUS));
 	mondrian_log_flush_now();
+	/*
+	 * The enable bits stay set after a transfer (the driver clears them,
+	 * the hardware does not), so a second vote would see the TCS busy and
+	 * bail out. Clear them and reuse the TCS.
+	 */
 	if (idle != 0) {
-		printf("MONDRIAN TOUCH: rpmh tcs0 busy, not voting\n");
-		return -1;
+		mondrian_tlmm_write(rsc, base + MONDRIAN_RSC_CMD_ENABLE, 0);
+		__builtin_arm_dsb(0xf);
 	}
 	for (i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
 		mondrian_tlmm_write(rsc, base + i * MONDRIAN_RSC_CMD_STEP +
